  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-saving protection and shelter assistance to IDPs in Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this CERF &#x2013; UFE allocation, UNHCR intends to provide a critical and timely life-saving assistance to respond to the current gaps of crisis-affected people in the North-West, Southeast and North-East (North Shan State) parts of Myanmar. The project will support 75,000 conflict and crisis affected people in the area of Protection (including through strengthened Protection Monitoring, PSEA trainings and information sharing and enhanced access to Community-based protection services.&#xa0;provision of community grants for community-based projects, and improved AAP), Sectoral&#xa0;Cash for vulnerable people with specific needs for protection outcome&#xa0;will also be provided. In addition&#xa0;68,500 people will be benefitted with in kind&#xa0;NFIs support and&#xa0;Cash for Shelter. Further&#xa0;Multi-Purpose cash grant shall be provided to 23,930 people&#xa0;to meet their most urgent basic needs- per HH calculation will be based on CWG endorsed grant value.</narrative>
  </description>
